  "worked_solution": "First, we take ${log}_{8}$ on both sides of the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{1-x} & ={3}^{x/2} \\\\ {log}_{8}\u2061({8}^{1-x}) & ={log}_{8}\u2061({3}^{x/2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}\u2061({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n1-x={log}_{8}\u2061({3}^{x/2})\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n1-x=\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}\u20613\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-x & =\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}\u20613 \\\\ 1 & =x+\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}\u20613 \\\\ x+\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}\u20613 & =1 \\\\ 2x+x{log}_{8}\u20613 & =2 \\\\ x(2+{log}_{8}\u20613) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{2+{log}_{8}\u20613}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the change of base formula, we have\n\n$$\n{log}_{8}\u2061(3)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(8)}\u22480.528\\,321.\n$$\n\nFinally,  we can approximate $x$ as \n\n$$\nx\u2248\\frac{2}{2+0.528\\,321}\u22480.791,\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
